.TH DEECURE-DESKTOP 1 "October 2026" "DeeCure 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deecure-desktop \- the DeeCure desktop app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deecure-desktop
.RB [ \-\-hidden ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deecure-desktop
opens the DeeCure window. It shows what the DeeCure agent found on this
computer: a health score, problems explained in plain English, and one page
for each part of the computer, such as performance, hardware, storage,
services, logs, networks, security, and privacy.
.PP
The app talks to the agent over a private socket in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/deecure/agent.sock .
The agent starts by itself when the app asks for it (systemd socket
activation). Everything stays on this computer.
.PP
Only one copy runs. Starting it again shows the window of the copy that runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start with only the tray icon, when the tray icon is turned on in
Settings and the desktop has a tray area. Otherwise the window opens as
usual. The login entry DeeCure writes for the tray uses this.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/deecure/deecure.db
The agent's history and findings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/deecure/desktop.json
The app's own settings, such as the tray icon.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.krisskad0.DeeCure.desktop
Starts DeeCure in the tray at login, while the tray icon is on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deecure (1)
.SH BUGS
Report problems at https://github.com/krisskad0/DeeCure/issues
